From 14c9e709b87f7cb46e4f37982462d9664ef03e7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:08:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Recycle bin per client: a deleted post can be restored

Deleting a post (the post page or the list's bulk delete) soft-deletes it: it leaves
every list, the approval links and the tools, and keeps its captions, media, notes and
approvals. The client's Recycle bin tab lists the deleted posts with who deleted them
and when, restores one or all, or deletes them for good. Nothing empties it on its own.

Post names stay unique with binned posts counted. A publish job already queued leaves a
binned post alone. An approval left with nothing to decide reminds nobody and closes
once overdue; a post restored after that comes back a Draft. An old link to a binned
post opens the bin, and the assets page names a binned post that uses a file.
Decision D20.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GAFd54RLsKcieieWCSQ4Cx
